        "original_id": "d55346de-c333-550f-aaae-832a091dc0ba",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Worthy S. Streator, James A. Garfield\n- Places: Streator, Illinois\n- Roles: physician, railroad developer, industrialist, entrepreneur, President of the United States\n- Events: Garfield's funeral, Garfield's assassination\n\nFacts:\n- Worthy Stevens Streator was born on October 16, 1816, and he was an American physician, railroad developer, industrialist, and entrepreneur.\n- James Abram Garfield was born on November 19, 1831, and he became the 20th President of the United States.\n- In 1881, James Abram Garfield served as President of the United States from March 4 until his assassination later that year.\n- In 1881, Worthy Stevens Streator was a pallbearer at James Abram Garfield's funeral.\n- The city of Streator, Illinois, was named after Worthy Stevens Streator.\n- James Abram Garfield died on September 19, 1881.\n- Worthy Stevens Streator died on March 6, 1902.",
